From 0eb1b6434f20f3568f8e64b522637be089529417 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: schoeremy <jeremyfroeb2007@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 19:57:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 65/65] nxhost: Nextendo's BCAT data for Splatoon 3, as a RomFS
 override and delivery cache

The Lobby and Hotlantis stayed "offline" although every NPLN call succeeded
and the STUN check got its answer. The game opens its BCAT delivery file
eu-default and got NotFound; next to "BcatSummaryNotFound" in the game's
strings sit "GamesyncInactive" and "NoUserHandle", which look like the
reasons for being offline.

Prelude-Nextendo downloads https://nextendo.network/api/bcat/<title id>, a
zip with ap-/eu-/jp-/us-default directories (summary.yml naming the fest,
*.pack.zs.enc), and installs it under romfs DebugUnderPilot/bcat. nexbcat
now does the same at start in Nextendo mode for Splatoon 3: download (public
API, no token), unpack the stored zip entries into
work/nextendo-bcat/romfs/DebugUnderPilot/bcat, layer it over the RomFS like
a mod, and keep the last good copy if the download fails. The BCAT service
also serves those directories through the delivery cache (enumerate, open,
read, size, MD5 digest), since the game asked the system for eu-default.
